    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Here's what I changed and why.\n\n## Summary\n\nTelephone is now stored and returned in E.164 form, with duplicate detection comparing E.164 values, and invalid numbers rejected with 400.\n\nThe E.164 conversion lives in one small, cohesive method so structural impact stays low \u2014 the two advice classes are tiny (low `WMC_other`), and I kept each edited method simple:\n\n**`OwnerTelephoneNormalizationAdvice`** \u2014 replaced the \"strip to exactly 10 digits\" rule with a static `toE164(...)`:\n- Keeps a leading `+` and its country code when present.\n- Otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0` from the national digits.\n- Strips spaces/dashes/brackets (all non-digits), and requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+`, else throws \u2192 400.\n- e.g. `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678`, `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456`, `12` \u2192 rejected.\n\n**`OwnerUniqueTelephoneAdvice`** \u2014 reuses `toE164(...)` and compares the resulting E.164 string directly against stored owners' E.164 telephones. It normalizes independently, so duplicate detection is correct regardless of advice ordering (matching the codebase's existing order-tolerant pattern; `toE164` is idempotent on already-E.164 values).\n\nTwo constraint relaxations were required so the `+`-prefixed value survives validation (both patterns previously demanded digits-only, which runs *after* normalization):\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 swapped the `^[0-9]{10}$` `@Pattern` and `@Digits` for `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` (JPA pre-persist validation).\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `telephone` pattern to `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` (generated-DTO `@Valid` on the controller).\n\nVerified: `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
